#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
tools/rush-submit-evidence — the BEST submission step for Rush LiveDev.

Replaces the ad-hoc submit code in livedev-bootstrap.sh with a single,
well-designed tool that handles every submission path:

  1. Validate the run dir before doing anything (no broken submissions).
  2. Generate a rich Markdown PR body with:
     - pass/fail badge
     - host fingerprint table
     - per-benchmark results table (parsed from manifest.json)
     - validation status
     - artifact bundle link
  3. Create a deterministic branch name (host + date + run-id).
  4. Copy results into benchmarks/results/<date>/<host>/.
  5. Commit with a structured, parseable message.
  6. Push the branch (using gh CLI or GH_TOKEN).
  7. Open or UPDATE a PR (dedup: if a PR already exists for this branch,
     update its body instead of creating a duplicate).
  8. Auto-label the PR (evidence, livedev, pass/fail).
  9. Upload the artifact bundle as a PR comment attachment (base64) or
     GitHub Actions artifact (if in CI).
 10. Print the PR URL.

Usage:
  python3 tools/rush-submit-evidence <run_dir> [--dry-run] [--submit-mode auto]
  python3 tools/rush-submit-evidence <run_dir> --submit-mode local
  python3 tools/rush-submit-evidence <run_dir> --submit-mode github
  python3 tools/rush-submit-evidence <run_dir> --submit-mode http --endpoint URL

Exit codes:
  0 — submission succeeded (or dry-run OK)
  1 — validation failed (broken run dir)
  2 — auth/push/PR failed
  3 — network error
"""

